  "kinds_comment": "Scavenger kinds: the name the game shows ('a hostile mob') and the fixed list of pages that count, by hand (first picked from the wiki's categories, approved 2026-10-21, then filled in where a category misses pages, as it did five helmets; a kind's key is the category it started from, and is what links and history records hold). Neither the build nor the game asks the wiki what is in a kind. Lists leave out overview pages (Food, Tree), mob combinations (jockeys), members a player wouldn't expect (Chicken in Nether mobs, Elytra in Tools), and joke, removed, education and fiction pages. also lists the few pages a Content checkbox hides that are still fair finds (Illusioner, Sprinting): reaching one counts, but par, Distance and the examples never go by them, so a route never ends on a page the box hides. build.py stops if a member or also page is no longer an article, a page is on both, or a kind has fewer than 5 members; report.py lists what each category holds that its list doesn't, for a new snapshot.",
  "disambiguation_categories": ["Disambiguation pages", "Version disambiguation pages"],
  "version_categories": ["Versions", "Development version lists", "Version disambiguation pages"],
  "version_title": "^(?:(?:Java Edition|Bedrock Edition(?: Preview| beta)?|Bedrock Dedicated Server|Bedrock Editor|Minecraft Education(?: Preview)?|Launcher|Preview) (?:\\d+\\.\\d|\\d\\dw\\d\\d[a-z])|\\d\\dw\\d\\d[a-z]|\\d+\\.\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)*(?:$| Snapshot |-(?:pre|rc|snap)\\d))",
  "versions_comment": "Version pages: articles and spin-off pages in a category ending in ' versions' or in one of these, but those with a topic or a family (the removed and unused features lists). Their history sections link them from almost every article, and they link to most of the pool, so they make any pair two clicks: build.py leaves them out of the data, with their subpages, and the game kills links to them and their redirects. Version disambiguation pages (1.18) go with them: nearly dead ends, whose links are nearly all to version pages. Relaxed lets version links live all the same, since navboxes already make its pairs par 1 or 2 and they barely change that, though par doesn't know the pages. version_title is a pattern (for Python and JavaScript alike) for the titles releases get, so that the game kills links to versions newer than the snapshot too, which no list can name: build.py stops if it matches a page in the data, or a redirect to one that a page links to.",
  "list_titles": [
    "Closed captions", "Bedrock Edition data values", "Java Edition data values", "Java Edition Flattening", "Block sound type",
    "Map item format", "Entity format", "Block tag (Java Edition)", "Item tag (Java Edition)", "Creative inventory", "Instant mining"
  ],
  "list_titles_comment": "List pages, left out like the version pages, with their subpages, even from a family: tables of game data that many articles link to and that link to much of the pool, so a route through one feels like a cheat, in every difficulty (hand-picked 2026-10-22 from the pages most often on a shortest route; Particles and Block states were kept on purpose). build.py stops if one is no longer an article.",
  "hubs": [
    "Minecraft", "Java Edition", "Bedrock Edition", "Edition", "Minecraft Education", "Commands", "Identifier", "Block", "Item",
    "Mob", "Biome", "Structure", "Overworld", "The Nether", "The End", "Player", "Creative", "Crafting", "Smelting", "Breaking",
    "Drops", "Renewable resource", "Food", "Tool", "Armor", "Weapon", "Ore", "Trading", "Enchantment", "Effect", "Advancement",
    "Achievement"
  ],
  "hubs_comment": "No hubs rule: links to these and their redirects are dead. Picked from the pages with the most incoming and outgoing links (report.py lists candidates), leaving out specific content (Diamond, Chest, Water…) that makes a fair target.",
  "core_namespaces": [
    "Media", "Special", "Talk", "User", "User talk", "Minecraft Wiki", "Minecraft Wiki talk", "Project", "Project talk",
    "File", "File talk", "Image", "Image talk", "MediaWiki", "MediaWiki talk", "Template", "Template talk",
    "Help", "Help talk", "Category", "Category talk", "Module", "Module talk", "Bucket", "Bucket talk", "Forum", "Forum talk"
  ],
  "namespaces_comment": "The ZIM holds articles and categories plus the wiki's own content namespaces (Tutorial, Dungeons…), and build.py adds those and their talk namespaces. Links into these other namespaces still appear on live pages, so they are listed by hand (from meta=siteinfo)."
}
